codex
The proxy currently sends health requests through Supabase session handling, so the endpoint needs an exact `/api/health` bypass. The installed Next.js guide also confirms that GET handlers are uncached by default; `Cache-Control: no-store` is sufficient with the current configuration.

I’ll use package.json for version and NODE_ENV for environment, documenting that preview builds report production. Backend owns the route and proxy, QA owns tests and docs, and an independent verifier owns final checks.

